---
description: Solo project docs and docs sync rules
alwaysApply: false
globs: docs/**,**/*.md
---

Project facts belong in project-local docs, not upstream templates:

- `docs/USER_GUIDE.md`
- `docs/PRODUCT.md`
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/CODING_GUIDE.md`
- `docs/TASKS.md`
- `docs/TASK_TEMPLATE.md`
- `docs/QUICK_TASK_TEMPLATE.md`
- `docs/tasks/T00x-*.md`

Project architecture facts belong in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. Coding standards and stack practices belong in `docs/CODING_GUIDE.md`. Solo task state belongs in `docs/TASKS.md` and `docs/tasks/`. Task IDs use `T001`, `T002`, … with files `docs/tasks/T001-short-name.md`. If `docs/TASKS.md` and a task doc disagree, trust the task doc and update `docs/TASKS.md`.

Do not infer project facts from upstream templates, copy root project state into templates, or treat template placeholders as facts.

`sync docs` has two jobs:

1. Replace init placeholders with inspected project facts.
2. Keep project-local docs accurate against inspected project contents.

`sync docs` and docs-only changes are direct updates when the request is clear. Do not require a proposal, verification step, or acceptance step. Finish by listing every changed document with a brief note.

After `protocol:init`, replace placeholder seed content with correct project-specific content. If any `TODO(ai-docs-sync)` notice or `{{PLACEHOLDER_NAME}}` placeholder is present, tell the user placeholders remain, do not treat placeholders as project facts, and replace them from inspected evidence.

When code changes affect APIs, commands, events, data schema, settings, user-visible behavior, coding standards, dependencies, stack practices, or top-level modules, sync the relevant project-local docs in the same change or explain why no docs sync is needed. Preserve paths, commands, code blocks, task IDs, status tokens, placeholder semantics, and technical names.

Upstream core and init seed templates stay English. Target-project docs follow `.protocol/protocol.json` language after localization, including `docs/TASK_TEMPLATE.md`, `docs/QUICK_TASK_TEMPLATE.md`, and `docs/CODING_GUIDE.md`. Do not rewrite historical task records under `docs/tasks/` only for localization unless they are otherwise being updated. For encoding and newline policy, read upstream `../shared/rule_docs/ENCODING.md` on demand.
